WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.334
-Welcome.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.370
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.474
We are coming at you
from Studio 6A

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.743
here in Rockefeller Plaza
in New York City.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.510
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:15.081
Well, guys, we are just one week
away from Election Day!

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.583
[ Applause ]

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.152
I can't believe it's that soon.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.753
I mean, it feels like
the last four years

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.755
have just really flown by!

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.390
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.358
Seriously, every morning
since 2016,

00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:28.761
Democrats have been carving
the days into the walls

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.730
like they're doing time
at Rikers Island.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.198
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.300
If Biden wins, Democrats are
gonna walk out of their houses

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.068
with an extra 50 pounds
of muscle

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:37.670
and a jug of toilet wine.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.873
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.441
That's right, we're just seven
days away from the election,

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:44.944
and just seven months
from knowing who won.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.079
That's exciting.
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:48.782
Yep. In seven days
we'll find out if Trump's

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:52.852
sticking around or getting
replaced like the Bachelorette.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.587
This week cannot go fast enough.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.656
If you're looking for ways
to pass the time,

00:00:56.656 --> 00:01:00.426
just ask Joe Biden to tell
one story from high school.

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:02.795
"My pal Skee-Ball and I
were on our way

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.297
to the sock hop, and..."

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:08.401
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.302
But seven days is still
a lot of time.

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:11.904
If you get in line to vote now,

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.639
there's a really good chance
you'll make it to the front

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:15.941
by November 3rd.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:17.943
Everyone's excited about
this election.

00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:20.046
I mean, check out how many
people have already voted.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.580
-We are one week out
from Election Day,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.016
and look at that number.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.818
More than 65 million ballots
already cast.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:29.055
-That's right, over 65 million
have already voted.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.824
And thanks to the Supreme Court,
almost 3 million of those

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.026
will be counted.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.594
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.495
These voting numbers
are incredible.

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:38.965
The United States could have
its highest election turnout

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.933
since 1908.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.169
You know 2020's been rough when
we're like,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.904
"Let's party like it's 1908!"

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.740
[ Laughter ]
[ Drumming march plays ]

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.376
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.078
Wow, I love that.

00:01:53.078 --> 00:01:55.214
1908 was a lot like 2020.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:57.583
The country was divided,
turnout was high,

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.518
and Bernie Sanders
lost in the primary.

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:01.854
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.357
A lot of groaners tonight, huh?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.292
Cheer up.
Come on, man.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.394
That's right, the U.S. is on
track for the highest election

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.995
turnout since 1908.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:13.466
That got me wondering, why were
so many people voting in 1908?

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.735
Well, when you compare today's
issues to back then,

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.136
it kind of makes sense.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.305
For example, in 2020,
voters want to stop

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.374
a global warming
catastrophe.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.409 line:0%
In 1908, voters wanted
to stop pollution

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.911 line:0%
from the four cars that existed.

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:29.315
In 2020, voters want to settle
things at the ballot box.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.150 line:0%
In 1908, voters wanted
to settle things

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.285 line:0%
by racing a donkey
and an elephant.

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:35.555
[ Laughter ]
And finally, in 2020,

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.023
voters complain
the election season

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.458
is like watching paint dry.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.359 line:0%
In 1908, voters said,
"Paint drying?

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:41.995
I got to check this out."

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.498
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.867
With the time running short
until the election,

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.803
both campaigns are going all out
and holding as many rallies

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.439
across the country as they can.
Listen to this.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.674
-An active day on the trail,
Joe Biden stopping in Georgia,

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:57.343
Kamala Harris in Nevada.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.811
The former President,
Barack Obama,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.380
campaigning for the
Democrats in Orlando, Florida.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.149
Jill Biden heads to Maine.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.184
The President hits a trio
of Midwest states --

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.452
Michigan, Wisconsin,

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.587
and Nebraska's Second
Congressional District.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.623
Vice President Mike Pence is
in the Carolinas today,

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.892
and the First Lady is
traveling to Pennsylvania.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.828
-Whew. Usually the only people
who travel this much

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.363
are salesmen and fugitives.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.932
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.833
Yep, Trump and Pence
are everywhere.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.234
Even the coronavirus was like,

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.404
"Guys, please, gimme a second
to catch up."

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:27.106
I think all the traveling
confused Trump,

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.375
'cause he bragged about saving
Nebraska's auto industry

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.045
and rescuing the great
dairy farms of Michigan.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.612
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:35.781
I'm not sure Trump's rallies are
really moving the needle.

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:38.117
It's hard to convince voters
you deserve a second term

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.187
when your speech has 42 mentions
of the word "plague."

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:43.355
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:45.691
But you can tell Trump's getting
tired 'cause at one rally

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.560
he just rolled out a television
and played a video

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.129
like a substitute teacher.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.064
"You know what's better than
reading 'Moby Dick'?

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:54.100
Watching 'Air Bud.'"

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.001
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:59.238
Listen to what's going on
with gym's in Newark.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.140 line:0%
-New restrictions aimed
at stopping a surge

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.677 line:0%
in coronavirus cases
take effect today in Newark.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.714 line:0%
Gyms and fitness centers are
under orders to shut down

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:11.350 line:0%
for 30 minutes every hour
for a deep cleaning.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.354
-30 minutes every hour?

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.622
The only person who's going to
get in shape is the janitor.

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:19.458
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.728
Already there's one creepy
employee who just walks up

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:24.363
to the machines and whispers,
"Bath time."

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:28.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.169
"Bath time."

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.037
[ Vocalizing ]
♪♪

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:34.974
♪ Bath time ♪
[ Vocalizing ]

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.175
♪ Bath time ♪

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.210
[ Vocalizing ]

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.279
♪ Bath time ♪
[ Vocalizing ]

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:41.314
Go, rap.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:42.615
-♪ Bath time, bath time ♪

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.183
♪ It's time to take a bath ♪

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.851
♪ It's time to get
some soap out ♪

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:47.687
♪ And then you wash your -- ♪

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:50.189
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.124
-I was waiting for you
to cut me off.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.092
Say, hey, hey!
-Whoa, whoa, whoa,

00:04:54.092 --> 00:04:55.427
this is a family show.

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:57.730
Sorry. Sorry,
I forgot to do that. Yeah.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.131
♪♪

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:01.634
[ Vocalizing ]
♪♪

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.835
-Wait.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.638
That's Billy Bob Thornton's
character on --

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.806
-Oh yeah, "Sling Blade."

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:10.943
-[ Mumbling ]

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.778
You --

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:14.346
-Bath time, mm-hmm.

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:16.215
-Mm-hmm, bath time.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.451
"You mind if I hang out
with your son

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.986
and be best friends with him?"

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.054
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:24.156
I don't know if you guys should
be hanging out in the woods.

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:26.025
No, I'm doing like --

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:29.361
[ Vocalizing ]
♪♪

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:34.434
[ Vocalizing ]

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.235
♪ Call me Mr. Bombastic ♪

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.937
♪ Mr. Fantastic ♪

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.338
[ Scatting ]

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.707
♪ Mr. Ro... ♪

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:44.610
♪ Bath time, duh-nuh-nuh-nuh,
bath time ♪

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.045
-It's not right.
-♪ Ro... ♪

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.946
-It's not right
without Higgins here.

00:05:47.946 --> 00:05:49.081
-♪ Bath time ♪

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:51.784
[ Vocalizing ]

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.886
♪ Now you got to
wash your -- time ♪

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:57.723
[ Vocalizing ]

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:00.760
-It's not right.
-It's not right, no.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.828
Oh yeah, that's right.
That's right.

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:05.531
Hey, I'm a little worried that
Newark Planet Fitness

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.634
is taking better precautions
than the coronavirus task force.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.736
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:11.971
Let's change gears.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.639
I heard about a billionaire
in California

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.842
who is feuding with
his neighbor.

00:06:16.842 --> 00:06:19.178
And recently, their fight
took an interesting turn.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:20.479
Watch this.

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:22.748 line:0%
-♪ Sit right back and
you'll hear a tale ♪

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.483 line:0%
♪ A tale of a fateful trip ♪

00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:26.485 line:0%
-Two neighbors in Laguna Beach,
California, they've been

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:28.454 line:0%
in a dispute over
a lawn sculpture.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:31.557 line:0%
So, billionaire Bill Gross,
he's been blaring

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.792 line:0%
the "Gilligan's Island"
theme song at all hours

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.995 line:0%
of the day and night in an
attempt to annoy the neighbors

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:39.332 line:0%
in hopes that they'll drop their
complaint over the sculpture.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.967
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:45.237
-So to recap, he annoyed
his neighbor by also

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:48.174
making himself listen to the
"Gilligan's Island" theme song.

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:49.842
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:52.110
He was like, "Sorry, I only
wanted to do it for three hours,

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.913
but it wound up being much
longer."

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.848
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.550
That's right.
[ Applause ]

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.218
[ Ding! ]

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.719
Bob Denver fans.

00:07:00.719 --> 00:07:02.021
♪♪

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:03.522
♪ I'm Bob Denver ♪

00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:05.157
[ Vocalizing ]

00:07:05.157 --> 00:07:09.061
♪ Bob Denver ♪
[ Vocalizing ]

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.829
I'll be honest,
I just think it's nice

00:07:10.829 --> 00:07:12.297
that we can still find
things to fight about

00:07:12.297 --> 00:07:14.633
besides the election.

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:17.136
And finally I saw that Four Loko
is coming out with

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:19.305
new bottled drinks called
Pregame.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:21.006
Here they are.

00:07:21.006 --> 00:07:22.942
-What?
-It's perfect for when you want

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.677
to pass out before
leaving the house.

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.178
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:27.813
To buy a bottle, you have
to show your ID

00:07:27.813 --> 00:07:29.448
and give an emergency contact.

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:30.849
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:32.584
That's right. You can either
drink it or just skip a step

00:07:32.584 --> 00:07:34.520
and put yourself
in the back of a police car.

